or);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Milk</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Vanilla extract</span></li></ul></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Chocolate Frosting</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">0.67</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cup</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Unsweetened cocoa powder</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">cups</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Powdered sugar</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-11378-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"11378\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Cake pan&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">Greased and ready for batter</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Mixing bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing ingredients</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing dry ingredients</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Electric mixer&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For creaming butter and sugar</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-11378-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-11378-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"11378\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Preparation</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C). This ensures your cake bakes evenly and rises beautifully.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a bowl, whisk together the flour, baking powder, and salt. This mix will give your cake the perfect structure.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In another bowl, cream the butter and sugar together until light and fluffy. This step adds air to your batter, making it light and tender.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Add the eggs one at a time, mixing well after each addition. Then, stir in the vanilla extract for that lovely flavor.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-4\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Alternate adding the dry ingredients and milk to the butter mixture. Mix until smooth and well combined. Don’t overmix; a few lumps are okay!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-5\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Pour the batter into a greased cake pan. Bake for 25-30 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Your kitchen will smell amazing!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-6\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Once baked, let the cake cool completely in the pan. This usually takes about an hour. Patience is key!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-7\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">In a bowl, beat the butter and cocoa powder together. Gradually add the powdered sugar and a splash of milk until creamy and smooth.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-11378-step-0-8\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Spread the chocolate frosting over the cooled cake. Make it as thick or thin as you like. Enjoy your delicious creation!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      \n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s what you’ll need to whip up a delightful vanilla <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">cake </a>with creamy chocolate frosting!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Vanilla-Cake-with-Chocolate-Frosting.webp\" alt=\"A collection of ingredients for vanilla cake chocolate frosting displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-11376\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Vanilla-Cake-with-Chocolate-Frosting.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Ingredients-for-Vanilla-Cake-with-Chocolate-Frosting-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>2 cups</strong> – All-purpose flour</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 ½ cups</strong> – Granulated sugar</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 tablespoon</strong> – Baking powder</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ teaspoon</strong> – Salt</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>½ cup</strong> – Unsalted butter, softened</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>3</strong> – Eggs</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>1 cup</strong> – Milk</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 teaspoons</strong> – Vanilla extract</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>⅔ cup</strong> – Unsweetened cocoa powder</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>2 cups</strong> – Powdered sugar</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-vanilla-cake-chocolate-frosting\"><strong>How to Make vanilla cake chocolate frosting</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful vanilla cake with chocolate frosting is a treat for any occasion! With a preparation time of about 20 minutes, a cooking time of 25-30 minutes, and a cooling time of 1 hour, you’ll have a delicious dessert ready to impress your friends and family.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Step-by-Step-Vanilla-Cake-with-Chocolate-Frosting.webp\" alt=\"Step-by-step process of making vanilla cake with chocolate frosting, including preheating the oven, preparing dry ingredients, creaming butter and sugar, and a finished frosted cake.\" class=\"wp-image-11377\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Step-by-Step-Vanilla-Cake-with-Chocolate-Frosting.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Step-by-Step-Vanilla-Cake-with-Chocolate-Frosting-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Preheat the Oven</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Preheat your oven to 350°F (175°C). This ensures your cake bakes evenly and rises beautifully.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Prepare the Dry Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, whisk together the flour, baking powder, and salt. This mix will give your cake the perfect structure.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Cream Butter and Sugar</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In another bowl, cream the butter and sugar together until light and fluffy. This step adds air to your batter, making it light and tender.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Add Eggs and Vanilla</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the eggs one at a time, mixing well after each addition. Then, stir in the vanilla extract for that lovely flavor.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 5: Combine Dry Ingredients and Milk</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Alternate adding the dry ingredients and milk to the butter mixture. Mix until smooth and well combined. Don’t overmix; a few lumps are okay!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 6: Bake the Cake</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pour the batter into a greased cake pan. Bake for 25-30 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the center comes out clean. Your kitchen will smell amazing!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 7: Cool the Cake</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Once baked, let the cake cool completely in the pan. This usually takes about an hour. Patience is key!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 8: Make the Chocolate Frosting</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a bowl, beat the butter and cocoa powder together. Gradually add the powdered sugar and a splash of milk until creamy and smooth.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 9: Frost the Cake</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Spread the chocolate frosting over the cooled cake. Make it as thick or thin as you like. Enjoy your delicious creation!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Dessert</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>American</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>20 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>30 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>60 minutes (cooling)</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>110 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Vegetarian</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Chilled or at room temperature</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-vanilla-cake-chocolate-frosting\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making vanilla cake chocolate frosting</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use room temperature ingredients for a smoother batter.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Don’t overmix; fold gently to keep the cake light and fluffy.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chill the chocolate frosting for easier spreading.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with different extracts for a unique flavor twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let the cake cool completely before frosting to prevent melting.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-vanilla-cake-chocolate-frosting\"><strong>How to Serve this vanilla cake chocolate frosting</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Top with fresh berries for a fruity twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve with a scoop of vanilla ice cream on the side.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Drizzle with caramel sauce for extra sweetness.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with a cup of coffee or tea for a cozy treat.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add sprinkles or nuts for a fun crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Slice and serve at birthday parties or celebrations.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You can make this cake ahead and store it easily:</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing vanilla cake chocolate frosting Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Allow the cake to cool completely before storing.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Wrap the cake tightly in plastic wrap or aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Store in an airtight container at room temperature for up to 3 days.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For longer storage, refrigerate the cake for up to a week.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing vanilla cake chocolate frosting</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Wrap the cooled cake in plastic wrap, then in aluminum foil.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Label with the date and type of cake.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Freeze for up to 3 months for best quality.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For frosting, store in an airtight container in the freezer.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating vanilla cake chocolate frosting</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw the cake in the refrigerator overnight.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>For a warm slice, microwave for 10-15 seconds.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Let frosting come to room temperature before using.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Re-whip frosting if it appears too firm after thawing.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. Can you put chocolate icing on a vanilla cake?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Absolutely! Chocolate icing pairs wonderfully with vanilla cake, creating a delightful contrast of flavors. The rich, creamy chocolate frosting enhances the light and fluffy vanilla cake, making it a popular choice for many dessert lovers.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What kind of frosting goes well with vanilla cake?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>While chocolate frosting is a classic choice, vanilla cake also pairs beautifully with cream cheese frosting, buttercream, or even fruit-flavored frostings like strawberry or lemon. Each option brings its own unique flavor profile to complement the vanilla base.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. What flavor cake goes best with chocolate frosting?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Chocolate frosting is incredibly versatile and can be paired with various cake flavors. However, it shines particularly well on vanilla, chocolate, and red velvet cakes, creating a rich and indulgent dessert experience.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. Do vanilla and chocolate go together?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, vanilla and chocolate are a classic combination! The sweet, creamy notes of vanilla beautifully balance the rich, deep flavors of chocolate, making them a perfect match in many desserts, including cakes, cookies, and ice creams.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We hope you’re as excited to try this vanilla cake with chocolate frosting as we are! It’s a simple, delightful treat that brings back sweet memories and creates new ones. So grab your ingredients, get baking, and enjoy every delicious bite. You deserve this little slice of happiness!</p>\n",
